--==============================================================================
-- MIREMAW -- SEVENTY-THREE PARTS, AND THE PERFORMANCE THAT WAS APPROVED WITH IT
--
-- The approval plinth (NestDais) and the billboard anchor are NOT here: they
-- belonged to the mockup, not to the creature. What is here is the approved
-- silhouette -- the hood and its three veins, four frond midribs, the ribbed
-- luminous throat, nostrils, eyelids, shoulder moss and the water details.
--
-- THE REST POSE IS AWAKE, AND THAT MATTERS.
--
-- The mockup was still running its eighteen-second loop when it was read, so
-- any single capture is a mid-blend phase that nobody approved. Both endpoints
-- were instead captured keyed to the mockup's OWN PreviewState attribute --
-- which publishes ASLEEP / WAKING / AWAKE / SETTLING -- at the frame closest to
-- that state's typical openness. So the two poses below are the approved ones,
-- measured, and the blend between them is not an interpretation of a
-- description.
--
-- The rig rests AWAKE because that is the pose the walk cycle has to work from.
-- MiremawSleep is one delta per seam; ParentAnim lerps each toward identity on
-- the wake scalar, so wake = 0 IS the approved sleeping pose and wake = 1 IS the
-- approved waking pose, with every value between them a real interpolation.
--==============================================================================
